<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine market makers exercise T-Bills option.</title>
<headline>Argentine market makers exercise T-Bills option.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine market makers Tuesday exercised an option for additional 91-day Letes, purchasing $5.61 million in Treasury bills, the Economy Ministry said.</p>
<p>Earlier in the day the ministry placed $250 million in 91-day Letes at a cut-off yield of 6.38 percent and a price of 983.8728. Market makers were given an option for an extra 10 percent in Letes.</p>
<p>((-Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
